{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Like a House on Fire"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Smooth Sailing"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes well organized texts about the application for a job in an international organization through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le18ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reported Speech and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use reported speech when you are saying (reporting)  what other people said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past'. You need to change the verb to the next past form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\u201d \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already eaten</span> .\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cWhere do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">live</span>?\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lived</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\""}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">I</span></span> didn't want to go.<li>Bill said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">he</span></span> didn't want to go."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You usually introduce reported questions with the verb to ask. Here are some examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The vet <span class=\"strong\">asked</span> (me) <span class=\"strong\">if</span>/<span class=\"strong\">whether</span>... (YES/NO questions)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The nurse <span class=\"strong\">asked</span> (me) <span class=\"strong\">why/when/where/what/how</span>... "}, {"type": "text", "content": "(question-word questions)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You may need to change pronouns and tense as well as time and place in reported questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The word order is like that of a normal statement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "(subject-verb-object)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sally said that you had declined the invitation to throw axes on Sunday because you had so much work to do. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She also intimated that you had thought axe throwing was a silly idea."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Later,a friend of mine told me that she had seen you having drinks at a bistro downtown. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " A tag question is a statement that is followed by a mini-question. You use a tag question to ask for confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tag questions are used to mean \u201cDo you agree?\u201d or \u201cIs that right?\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The basic structure is:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" positive statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"negative tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your project is due tomorrow,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't it?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" negative statement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"positive tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You're not interested in leaving,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The tag repeats the auxiliary verb (or main verb when <span class=\"italic\">be</span>) from the statement and changes it to negative or positive."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our friendship is worth fighting for, isn't it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, I don't want us to be like two ships passing in the night, do you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've always been able to be honest with each other, haven't we?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ships that pass in the night"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people who \u200bmeet\u200b once or \u200btwice by \u200bchance for a \u200bshort \u200btime then do not \u200bsee each other again"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't want us to be like two ships passing in the night, do you? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use in an e-mail to describe emotions and behaviors."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mistaken identity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make an error about who someone is"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thought that it might have been a case of mistaken identity"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "workload"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of work assigned to or expected from a worker in a specified time period"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You spent most of the time on your cellphone, complaining about your workload."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cherish "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remember or hold an idea, belief, etc in a deeply felt way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I cherish our friendship and the memories we have shared."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to intimate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to suggest something in an indirect way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She also intimated that you had thought axe throwing was a silly idea."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le18ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "In pairs, brainstorm all the reasons people have a falling out with friends"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a role play where two friends have a falling out."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The dialogue should be at least 3 minutes long."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Set the scenario and use Tag questions to clarify information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "At the end of the role play, classmates offer advice on how to possibly resolve the argument."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brain storm situations which people have conflicts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I role play a dialogue with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for clarification. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give advice to classmates to help resolve conflicts."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about emotions, personal qualities and behavior."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about how to react to things going wrong."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write a short email."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you have a friend that you don't see as much as you used to? What happened?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you usually discuss your relationship and feelings? Why or why not?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Writing Spot: Tell it like it is!"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Vanessa is frustrated and <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">perplexed </span>by Peter's recent behavior. She writes